 "findings": [
  "Pooled across every state and territory (federal elections 2019, 2022, 2025): where Labor governed the state, federal Labor's swing there was +0.9 points relative to the national swing compared with states under the Coalition (permutation p = 0.47): no sign that voters punish their state government at federal elections, and if anything the opposite.",
  "Within each state (when the state government changed party between federal elections): +0.8 points (p = 0.42), from 7 changes of government.",
  "Victoria: Labor governed the state at all three, so Victoria cannot answer this on its own; its deviations from the national swing were 2019 +2.5, 2022 -2.0, 2025 -1.6 points.",
  "Same party at both levels: +0.80 points per unit (positive would mean a state government of the federal government's party helps it federally).",
  "Small sample (8 jurisdictions x 3 elections); adding 2004-2013 from the AEC files would more than double it."
 ]
